{
  "profile": 1,
  "comment": "THE SENSOR REGISTRY — one row per declared check, and the whole definition of that check: the command, the cadence, the bound, the consecutive count, the issue's kind and area, whether the check owns the closing, and the fields its condition fingerprint is derived from. `threshold` is the bound under `comparison` (`greater-than`, `below-floor`, `boolean`, or `baseline-multiple`, where the recorded baseline is multiplied by the threshold) — and a row whose score multiplies a path's size by how often it changed sits above the largest file it watches, so one change of a path it merely contains is not a condition (issue #665). `maxFilings` is the most conditions one run of one row may file: the registry's value bounds every row, a row may declare its own, and what a run does not file leaves as one summary item, so a mis-fitted bound costs one item instead of one per condition it happens to hold (issue #666). A measurement is one whitespace-free token, so the issue's own marker line can be parsed. `labels` is the set of fixed vocabulary values every issue this registry files carries — each named here rather than in the engine (design D12). A second project adapts this file (and tools/tooling.json) and edits no engine file (design D9, D12).",
  "namespace": "sensor",
  "labels": {
    "status": "open",
    "source": "ci"
  },
  "escalation": {
    "comment": "A condition that keeps returning is a specification or design problem, not an implementation one, so past `maxRecurrences` reopenings the check stops reopening and hands the issue to a person (design D6). The two labels are the whole label write of an escalation, and neither authorises automated work.",
    "maxRecurrences": 3,
    "labels": ["agent/needs-decision", "status/on-hold"]
  },
  "record": {
    "comment": "A row that ran and was green has no condition issue to carry its verdict, so its measurements go to one record issue per row: filed on the first such clear, never closed, and carrying this `status` so no work selector may take it (issue #257).",
    "status": "on-hold"
  },
  "maxFilings": 10,
  "rows": [
    {
      "id": "build-duration",
      "cmd": "tools/sensors/metrics/build-duration.sh",
      "cron": "0 3 * * *",
      "threshold": 1.5,
      "comparison": "baseline-multiple",
      "consecutive": 2,
      "class": "improvement",
      "category": "build-and-harness",
      "lifecycle": "file+close",
      "input": "build/gate-timings.json",
      "fingerprint": { "fields": ["job"] }
    },
    {
      "id": "package-size",
      "cmd": "tools/sensors/metrics/package-size.sh",
      "cron": "0 4 * * *",
      "threshold": 1.1,
      "comparison": "baseline-multiple",
      "consecutive": 2,
      "class": "improvement",
      "category": "build-and-harness",
      "lifecycle": "file+close",
      "input": "app/build/outputs/apk/mobile/debug/app-mobile-debug.apk",
      "fingerprint": { "fields": ["artifact"] }
    },
    {
      "id": "hotspot",
      "cmd": "tools/sensors/hotspot-report.sh",
      "cron": "0 5 * * 1",
